Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese save information
Applies after 0061-japanese-built-text.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The Japanese CONTINUE texts hold their values ({STR_VAR_1}, {STR_VAR_2}) and
counters: as the Japanese ROM does, the main menu fills the string vars and prints
each line whole at that ROM's x (the international code printed the values apart
and left the vars unset, so StringExpandPlaceholders ran on an empty buffer and
the main menu hung with a save present). The start menu's save information takes
that ROM's window, line spacing and left-aligned values, with the counter words
after the badge and Pokédex counts (BufferSaveMenuText); the start menu window is
a tile narrower and the main and start menus' entries a pixel lower, as there.
Other languages are unchanged.

